# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasCleanStart
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasCleanStart> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasCleanStart> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnectFlag> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasCleanStart> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasCleanStart> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnectVariableHeader> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasCleanStart> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasCleanStart> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Clean Start flag in CONNECT Flags. 1 requests a new Session; 0 continues an existing Session if present."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasCleanStart> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Clean Start"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasCleanStart> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If a CONNECT packet is received with Clean Start is set to 1, the Client and Server MUST discard any existing Session and start a new Session."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasCleanStart> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If a CONNECT packet is received with Clean Start set to 0 and there is a Session associated with the Client Identifier, the Server MUST resume communications with the Client based on state from the existing Session."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasCleanStart> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If a CONNECT packet is received with Clean Start set to 0 and there is no Session associated with the Client Identifier, the Server MUST create a new Session."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasClientID
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasClientID> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasClientID> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasClientID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#Client> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasClientID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasClientID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The MQTT Client identifier used when connecting to an MQTT Broker."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasClientID> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MQTT Client identifier"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasClientID> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The ClientID MUST be a UTF-8 Encoded String."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasClientID> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The ClientID MUST be used by Clients and by Servers to identify state that they hold relating to this MQTT Session between the Client and the Server."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnackFlag
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnackFlag> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnackFlag> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnackFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnackVariableHeader> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnackFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnackFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "CONNACK Acknowledge Flags byte. In MQTT 5.0 only Session Present (bit 0) is used; other bits are reserved."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnackFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Connack Flag"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnackFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Byte 1 is the \"Connect Acknowledge Flags\". Bits 7-1 are reserved and MUST be set to 0."@en .
