# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnectFlag
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnectFlag> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnectFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnectVariableHeader> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnectFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#unsignedByte> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnectFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "CONNECT Flags byte encoding User Name/Password/Will/Clean Start fields; reserved bit MUST be 0."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnectFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Connect Flags"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnectFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Bit 0 = Reserved; Bit 1 = Clean Start; Bit 2 = Will Flag; Bit 3 und 4 = Will QoS; Bit 5 = Will Retain; Bit 6 = Password Flag; Bit 7 = User Name Flag."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnectFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The Server MUST validate that the reserved flag in the CONNECT packet is set to 0."@en .
