<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasFilterPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasFilterPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The MQTT Topic Filter pattern as a string (e.g., 'sensor/+/temp' or 'fabrik/zentrierung/#')."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasFilterPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MQTT Topic Filter pattern"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasFilterPattern> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An MQTT topic filter used in subscriptions to match topic names. A filter pattern may include the single-level wildcard '+' and the multi-level wildcard '#'."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasFixedHeaderFlag
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasFixedHeaderFlag> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasFixedHeaderFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#PublishFixedHeader> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasFixedHeaderFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#unsignedByte> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasFixedHeaderFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fixed Header flags nibble (bits 3..0 of byte 1). Packet-type-specific reserved/required flag pattern in MQTT 5.0."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasFixedHeaderFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "FixedHeader flag"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasFixedHeaderFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Where a flag bit is marked as “Reserved”, it is reserved for future use and MUST be set to the value listed."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasHostAddress
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasHostAddress> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasHostAddress> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasHostAddress> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#Broker> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasHostAddress> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasHostAddress> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The hostname or IP address of an MQTT Broker."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasHostAddress> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "MQTT Broker host"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasHostAddress> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Examples: localhost, 127.0.0.1, mqtt.example.com, 192.168.0.10"@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasKeepAlive
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnectVariableHeader> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#unsignedShort> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Keep Alive in CONNECT variable header. Two Byte Integer seconds defining maximum time between Client Control Packets."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Keep Alive" .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If Keep Alive is non-zero and in the absence of sending any other MQTT Control Packets, the Client MUST send a PINGREQ packet."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If the Keep Alive value is non-zero and the Server does not receive an MQTT Control Packet from the Client within one and a half times the Keep Alive time period, it MUST close the Network Connection to the Client as if the network had failed."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumPacketSize
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumPacketSize> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumPacketSize> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProperty> .
