_:genid138 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
_:genid136 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumPacketSize> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#unsignedInt> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumPacketSize> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Maximum Packet Size Property. Four Byte Integer (non-zero) limiting maximum MQTT packet size accepted."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumPacketSize> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Maximum Packet Size"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumPacketSize> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "39 (0x27) Byte, Identifier of the Maximum Packet Size. Followed by a Four Byte Integer representing the Maximum Packet Size the Client is willing to accept. If the Maximum Packet Size is not present, no limit on the packet size is imposed beyond the limitations in the protocol as a result of the remaining length encoding and the protocol header sizes."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumQoS
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumQoS> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumQoS> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumQoS> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumQoS> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnackProperties> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumQoS> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#unsignedByte> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumQoS> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Maximum QoS Property. Byte specifying the highest QoS level supported by the Server."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumQoS> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Maximum QoS"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumQoS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A Server that does not support QoS 1 or QoS 2 PUBLISH packets MUST still accept SUBSCRIBE packets containing a Requested QoS of 0, 1 or 2."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumQoS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If a Client receives a Maximum QoS from a Server, it MUST NOT send PUBLISH packets at a QoS level exceeding the Maximum QoS level specified."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMaximumQoS> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If a Server does not support QoS 1 or QoS 2 PUBLISH packets it MUST send a Maximum QoS in the CONNACK packet specifying the highest QoS it supports."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContent
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ApplicationMessage> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Application message content carried by PUBLISH. Conceptual higher-level view of the PUBLISH payload."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Application Message content"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Example message content:\r\n- container field: data\r\n- encoding: UTF-8\r\n- content type: text/csv\r\n- delimiter: ;\r\n- fields: RFID; JobStart; JobEnd; Correction_X; Correction_Y; Correction_Z; Sensor; Actuator\r\n\r\nExample value:\r\nRFID;JobStart;JobEnd;Correction_X;Correction_Y;Correction_Z;Sensor;Actuator\r\nRFID_87A3F1;2025-12-03T09:15:02.120Z;2025-12-03T09:15:02.520Z;-0.44;-0.15;+0.10;Sensor1;Actuator1"@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentDelimiter
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentDelimiter> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentDelimiter> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentDelimiter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ApplicationMessage> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentDelimiter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentDelimiter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The delimiter used to separate fields in the Application Message content."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentDelimiter> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Application Message content delimiter"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageContentDelimiter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> ";"@en .
