<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageExpiryInterval> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Message Expiry Interval Property. Four Byte Integer seconds defining PUBLISH message lifetime."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageExpiryInterval> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Message Expiry Interval"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasMessageExpiryInterval> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "2 (0x02) Byte, Identifier of the Message Expiry Interval. Followed by the Four Byte Integer representing the Message Expiry Interval in seconds. If present, the Four Byte value is the lifetime of the Application Message in seconds. If absent, the Application Message does not expire."@en .
