_:genid174 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasPropertyLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasPropertyLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Property Length field preceding a Properties collection. Variable Byte Integer giving total length in bytes of following properties."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasPropertyLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Property Length is encoded as a Variable Byte Integer. The Property Length does not include the bytes used to encode itself, but includes the length of the Properties. If there are no properties, this MUST be indicated by including a Property Length of zero."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasPropertyLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has MQTT Property Length"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasPropertyLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The length of Properties in the DISCONNECT packet Variable Header encoded as a Variable Byte Integer. If the Remaining Length is less than 2, a value of 0 is used."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasPropertyLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The length of the Properties in the PUBACK packet Variable Header encoded as a Variable Byte Integer. If the Remaining Length is less than 4 there is no Property Length and the value of 0 is used."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasPropertyLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The length of the Properties in the UNSUBACK packet Variable Header encoded as a Variable Byte Integer."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasPropertyLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The length of the Properties in the Will Properties encoded as a Variable Byte Integer."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolName
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolName> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolName> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnectVariableHeader> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Protocol Name in CONNECT. UTF-8 string that MUST equal 'MQTT' for MQTT 5.0."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Protocol Name"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The protocol name MUST be the UTF-8 String \"MQTT\". If the Server does not want to accept the CONNECT, and wishes to reveal that it is an MQTT Server it MAY send a CONNACK packet with Reason Code of 0x84 (Unsupported Protocol Version), and then it MUST close the Network Connection."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolVersion
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolVersion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolVersion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnectVariableHeader> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#unsignedByte> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Protocol Version in CONNECT. One-byte value that MUST be 5 for MQTT 5.0."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Protocol Version"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProtocolVersion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If the Protocol Version is not 5 and the Server does not want to accept the CONNECT packet, the Server MAY send a CONNACK packet with Reason Code 0x84 (Unsupported Protocol Version) and then MUST close the Network Connection."@en .
