<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasReceiveMaximum> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#unsignedShort> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasReceiveMaximum> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Receive Maximum Property. Two Byte Integer (non-zero) limiting concurrent QoS 1/2 PUBLISH in-flight."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasReceiveMaximum> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Receive Maximum"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasReceiveMaximum> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "33 (0x21) Byte, Identifier of the Receive Maximum. Followed by the Two Byte Integer representing the Receive Maximum value. It is a Protocol Error to include the Receive Maximum value more than once or for it to have the value 0."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRemainingLength
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRemainingLength> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRemainingLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#FixedHeader> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRemainingLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#byte> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRemainingLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The Remaining Length is a Variable Byte Integer that represents the number of bytes remaining within the current Control Packet, including data in the Variable Header and the Payload. The Remaining Length does not include the bytes used to encode the Remaining Length. The packet size is the total number of bytes in an MQTT Control Packet, this is equal to the length of the Fixed Header plus the Remaining Length."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRemainingLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This is the length of the Variable Header (plus the length of the Payload), encoded as a Variable Byte Integer."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRemainingLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Remaining Length of MQTT Control Packet "@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRemainingLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "PUBACK: This is the length of the Variable Header, encoded as a Variable Byte Integer."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRemainingLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "PUBLISH: This is the length of Variable Header plus the length of the Payload, encoded as a Variable Byte Integer."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestProblemInformation
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestProblemInformation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestProblemInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestProblemInformation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestProblemInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnectProperties> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestProblemInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestProblemInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Request Problem Information Property in CONNECT. Byte 0/1 indicating whether the Server should include Reason String/User Properties on errors."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestProblemInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Request Problem Information"@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestResponseInformation
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnectProperties> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Request Response Information Property in CONNECT. Byte 0/1 indicating whether the Server should return Response Information in CONNACK."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Request Response Information"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRequestResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A value of 0 indicates that the Server MUST NOT return Response Information."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasResponseInformation
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnackProperties> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Response Information Property. UTF-8 string providing response metadata for request/response patterns."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Response Information"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasResponseInformation> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "25 (0x19) Byte, Identifier of the Request Response Information. Followed by a Byte with a value of either 0 or 1.  A value of 0 indicates that the Server MUST NOT return Response Information. If the value is 1 the Server MAY return Response Information in the CONNACK packet."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAsPublished
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAsPublished> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAsPublished> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionOption> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAsPublished> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#SubscriptionEntry> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAsPublished> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAsPublished> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Retain As Published subscription option. If 1, forwarded messages keep the original RETAIN flag."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAsPublished> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Retain As Published"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAsPublished> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If the value of Retain As Published subscription option is set to 0, the Server MUST set the RETAIN flag to 0 when forwarding an Application Message regardless of how the RETAIN flag was set in the received PUBLISH packet. If the value of Retain As Published subscription option is set to 1, the Server MUST set the RETAIN flag equal to the RETAIN flag in the received PUBLISH packet."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAvailable
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnackProperties> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Retain Available Property in CONNACK. Byte 0/1 indicating whether retained messages are supported."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Retain Available"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A Client receiving Retain Available set to 0 from the Server MUST NOT send a PUBLISH packet with the RETAIN flag set to 1."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainAvailable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If a Server receives a CONNECT packet containing a Will Message with the Will Retain set to 1, and it does not support retained messages, the Server MUST reject the connection request. It SHOULD send CONNACK with Reason Code 0x9A (Retain not supported) and then it MUST close the Network Connection."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainFlag
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainFlag> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasFixedHeaderFlag> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#PublishFixedHeader> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "True if the message should be retained on the MQTT Broker."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RETAIN flag"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If the RETAIN flag is 0 in a PUBLISH packet sent by a Client to a Server, the Server MUST NOT store the message as a retained message and MUST NOT remove or replace any existing retained message."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If the RETAIN flag is set to 1 in a PUBLISH packet sent by a Client to a Server, the Server MUST replace any existing retained message for this topic and store the Application Message."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainHandling
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainHandling> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainHandling> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSubscriptionOption> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainHandling> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#SubscriptionEntry> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainHandling> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#unsignedByte> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainHandling> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Retain Handling subscription option. Two-bit field: 0=send retained, 1=send retained only if subscription new, 2=do not send retained."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainHandling> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Retain Handling"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainHandling> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If Retain Handling is set to 0 the Server MUST send the retained messages matching the Topic Filter of the subscription to the Client."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainHandling> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If Retain Handling is set to 1 then if the subscription did not already exist, the Server MUST send all retained message matching the Topic Filter of the subscription to the Client, and if the subscription did exist the Server MUST NOT send the retained messages."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasRetainHandling> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If Retain Handling is set to 2, the Server MUST NOT send the retained messages."@en .
# 
# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasServerKeepAlive
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasServerKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasServerKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasServerKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasServerKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnackProperties> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasServerKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#unsignedShort> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasServerKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Server Keep Alive Property in CONNACK. Two Byte Integer seconds overriding the Client Keep Alive for this connection."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasServerKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Server Keep Alive"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasServerKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If the Server does not send the Server Keep Alive, the Server MUST use the Keep Alive value set by the Client on CONNECT."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasServerKeepAlive> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If the Server sends a Server Keep Alive on the CONNACK packet, the Client MUST use this value instead of the Keep Alive value the Client sent on CONNECT."@en .
# 
