# https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSessionPresentFlag
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSessionPresentFlag> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSessionPresentFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasConnackFlag> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSessionPresentFlag> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSessionPresentFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#ConnackVariableHeader> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSessionPresentFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSessionPresentFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Session Present flag in CONNACK. If 1, a prior Session exists and is resumed."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSessionPresentFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has Session Present Flag"@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSessionPresentFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If the Server accepts a connection with Clean Start set to 0 and the Server has Session State for the ClientID, it MUST set Session Present to 1 in the CONNACK packet, otherwise it MUST set Session Present to 0 in the CONNACK packet. In both cases it MUST set a 0x00 (Success) Reason Code in the CONNACK packet."@en .
<https://www.w3id.org/MQTT4SSN-Ontology#hasSessionPresentFlag> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "If the Server accepts a connection with Clean Start set to 1, the Server MUST set Session Present to 0 in the CONNACK packet in addition to setting a 0x00 (Success) Reason Code in the CONNACK packet."@en .
